We built SmithDB, a database designed specifically for agent observability workloads that now powers many parts of LangSmith. Agent traces can contain tens of thousands of intermediate spans and large, unbounded payloads, which are challenging for traditional data infrastructure to handle due to longer agent run times and growing LLM context windows.

SmithDB delivers up to 12 times performance improvements across key access patterns for agent observability. The development involved overcoming engineering challenges, and a detailed story is shared in a blog. If you're a systems engineer interested in building the future of agent observability, reach out.

@LangChain: "Just announced at Interrupt! SmithDB. Agent traces have outgrown the databases built to hold them. That’s why we built SmithDB, a purpose-built distributed database for agent observability."

